  "title": "Erdős Problem #650",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(m)$ be such that if $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ has $\\lvert A\\rvert=m$ then every interval in $[1,\\infty)$ of length $2N$ contains $\\geq f(m)$ many distinct integers $b_1,\\ldots,b_r$ where each $b_i$ is divisible by some $a_i\\in A$, where $a_1,\\ldots,a_r$ are distinct.\nEstimate $f(m)$. In particular is it true that $f(m)\\ll m^{1/2}$?",
